{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba players.py | tail -40\ncat legs_log.md'","aggregated_output":"    46\t    move(env, 3, 7)\n    47\t\n    48\t    # Approach the lower cross from above-left and launch it right.\n    49\t    move(env, 2, 3)\n    50\t    move(env, 3, 7)\n    51\t    move(env, 2, 2)\n    52\t    move(env, 4)\n    53\t\n    54\t    # Both crosses now match their outlines; fill the avatar's outline.\n    55\t    move(env, 1, 2)\n    56\t    move(env, 4, 5)\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef play_level_4(env):\n    60\t    # Launch the second controlled object through the barrier.\n    61\t    move(env, 4, 3)\n    62\t    move(env, 2)\n    63\t    select_object(env, 30, 48)\n    64\t    move(env, 2, 3)\n    65\t    move(env, 3)\n    66\t    move(env, 1)\n    67\t\n    68\t    # The lower object launches the cross back into the upper room.\n    69\t    select_object(env, 30, 30)\n    70\t    move(env, 1, 2)\n    71\t    move(env, 3, 4)\n    72\t    move(env, 2, 3)\n    73\t    move(env, 4)\n    74\t\n    75\t    # Shift the cross right, then launch it upward to its outline.\n    76\t    move(env, 2)\n    77\t    move(env, 4, 6)\n    78\t    move(env, 1, 7)\n    79\t\n    80\t    # Park both controlled objects in the small outlines.\n    81\t    move(env, 2, 3)\n    82\t    move(env, 4, 5)\n    83\t    select_object(env, 27, 57)\n    84\t    move(env, 4, 4)\n    85\t    move(env, 1)\n# Level 1: reproduced raw-frame observations\n\nAll experiments used fresh level-entry clones via the local harness, perception\ncomponents, and public frame/step/clone methods. No external sources were used.\n\n- Initial outlined objects have centers (x,y)=(19,31) and (28,31).\n  Default action_deltas and separate one-step replays identify keys 1,2,3,4\n  as up,down,left,right: the first object moves three pixels; the second stays.\n- Clicking (28,31) transfers the black center/control to the second object.